  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that the compound 3beta-(alpha-L-rhamnopyranosyloxy)-1beta,5beta,11alpha,14beta,19beta-pentahydroxy-5beta-card-20(22)-enolide may interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through multiple indirect pathways. It is identified as a target of Thrombopoietin, which itself is a target of a second compound, and both of these are targets of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. Additionally, the compound is also identified as a target of DNA polymerase iota, which is a target of another compound that also targets the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. These findings suggest that the compound may exert its effects through a network of molecular interactions, potentially involving epigenetic regulation. The evidence is consistent with the compound acting as a modulator of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated. The strength of the evidence is moderate, with varying scores across the different paths, indicating that the relationship is supported but not definitively established.",
